- op: discuss  # 3bd6
  at: '2026-11-18T16:57:22Z'  # 3bd6
  by: agent  # 3bd6
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3bd6
  clock: 3  # 3bd6
  nonce: 3bd6  # 3bd6
  message: "ROOT CAUSE FOUND (2026-11-18 ~17:30Z), fix not yet made. With HYPERGUMBO_SCIP_PYTHON=1 exported, smart-test of test_vcs_ignored_untracked.py, test_cli_run_behavior_map.py and test_unmodeled_alias_shapes.py fails 21 tests DETERMINISTICALLY, including both cases filed here (test_no_graph_node; the alias 'NOT CONFIRMED: ... calls into 2 module(s)' text) and every non-reproducing campaign-3/4 miss among those files (test_run_behavior_map_tolerates_unreadable_file_end_to_end, test_the_plain_shape_keeps_its_credit, alias S5L/S6b). A clean company run of 251 files failed 3 of them with scip/scip_python-origin nodes in the output and a rust-analyzer fallback warning. MECHANISM: cli.py (~line 3606) writes os.environ[HYPERGUMBO_SCIP_PYTHON / HYPERGUMBO_RUST_ANALYZER] for --backend, and test_backend_cli_flag.py's autouse fixtures use monkeypatch.delenv(VAR, raising=False), which records nothing when the variable is absent, so a value main() then writes outlives the test (test_present_and_available_sets_the_transport sets it to 1). No conftest resets these variables. NOT YET SHOWN: a two-file sequential repro (test_backend_cli_flag.py then the victims, -n 0) passed 118/118, so the exact leaking test is not pinned. FIX PLANNED: an autouse fixture restoring os.environ after every test in each package conftest (plus the root one), and test_backend_cli_flag.py's fixtures recording absence properly."  # 3bd6
